From 80aadea3814e66658ed5ee40dcfde1bebb9dc5ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cindy Krafft <cynthiacondra@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 02:49:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Count insert-state residues as inserts in
 p7_Null2_ByTrace()

The vector implementations of p7_Null2_ByTrace() (SSE, NEON, VMX)
added every residue emitted by a model state to the match cell of the
state's node, so residues emitted by insert states were scored with the
match emission odds of node k instead of the insert odds (1.0; insert
emission scores are 0 in a configured profile). The state type was
computed in 2008 and never used; the 2016 -Wall cleanup commented it
out as unneeded. The generic p7_GNull2_ByTrace() counts inserts
separately, and the vector code already sums the I cells with odds 1.0.

p7_Null2_ByTrace() sets the null2 correction for domains in regions
that go to stochastic traceback clustering, so bit scores, bias columns
and E-values of those domains and their sequences changed. On 500
sequences emitted from fn3, the SSE and generic null2 vectors agreed on
every domain without insert states and differed (up to 1.2 in log
odds) on all 469 domains with insert states. On human Swiss-Prot
searched with the tutorial fn3 and Pkinase models, 19 sequence scores
move by up to 0.7 bits (E-values by up to 1.75-fold).

Adds utest_null2_trace() to the SSE null2 test driver, comparing the
two implementations on profile-emitted traces; it fails without this
change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TaHntBDKuZJpMAAMenkC44
